    "q-129657": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129657",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Suppose that $f(x,y,z)$ is a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(1,2,3)=6,\\,{f}_{x}(1,2,3)=6,\\,{f}_{y}(1,2,3)=3,\\,{f}_{z}(1,2,3)=2.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,2,3)$ estimate the value of $f(1.08,1.93,3.05)$",
      "worked_solution": "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,2,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,2,3)+∇f(1,2,3)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z-3⟩ \\\\  & =6+⟨{f}_{x}(1,2,3),{f}_{y}(1,2,3),{f}_{z}(1,2,3)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z-3⟩ \\\\  & =6+⟨6,3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-2,z-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(1.08,1.93,3.05)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=1.08,$ $y=1.93,$ and $z=3.05$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.08,1.93,3.05) & ≈6+⟨6,3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨1.08-1,1.93-2,3.05-3⟩ \\\\  & =6+⟨6,3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨0.08,-0.07,0.05⟩ \\\\  & =6+6(0.08)+3(-0.07)+2(0.05) \\\\  & =6+0.48-0.21+0.1 \\\\  & =6.37\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
